{
  "summary": "Tracks in-flight manual P2P connection attempts in `CConnman` using a set of pending destination keys to prevent duplicate connections. When `OpenNetworkConnection()` initiates a manual connection, it registers the target in `m_manual_connection_in_progress` and clears it upon exit using an RAII guard. Concurrent attempts to dial the same numeric address or raw hostname string are rejected while the first attempt is pending.",
  "problem": "Concurrent manual connection attempts to the same target—such as overlapping `-connect` and `-addnode` startup arguments or concurrent `addnode onetry` invocations—race past existing duplicate checks. Because existing checks only verify connected peers already present in `m_nodes`, multiple connections to the same remote peer can be established before either completes.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description fixes #5299, an open issue titled 'Initial connection management' dating back to 2014.",
    "PR description: '-connect and -addnode can attempt the same manual connection concurrently during startup. The existing duplicate checks cannot see a peer until it has been added to m_nodes, so both attempts can pass and open connections.'"
